WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.410
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:10.800
EWA DUERR: Welcome to the
session on cloud automation

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.840
for Industrie 4.0.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.070
My name is Ewa Dueer.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:18.960
And I am a product obsolete for
Cloud AI EMEA Engineering team

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:19.500
in Munich.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:26.570
One of Google's primary
goals is to democratize

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:30.860
AI and automation and make
it easy and accessible

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.890
for all industries.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:37.940
Our vision is to
harness the power of AI

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:41.540
for the industry across
multiple verticals--

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.630
retail, logistics,
manufacturing, automotive,

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:46.610
and many others.

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:49.970
However, before we deep
dive into that vision,

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:52.130
I want to get us
started by looking

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:54.710
at the state of the
automation today.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:02.900
Automation today it is
only economical at scale.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:05.840
The upfront costs of
integration are huge,

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:09.190
and the results are inflexible
to changes in workflows.

00:01:12.052 --> 00:01:17.510
However, there is a new
trend emerging on the market.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:21.700
A new generation of
collaborative robots

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:26.590
are making the automation
much more affordable.

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:30.970
They are equipped with modern
sensors and software layers

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:32.260
that are easy to program.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:37.040
This new generation
of robots are

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:42.050
useful in unpredictable
environments and work side

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:43.475
by side with humans.

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:50.740
We still have to tackle
a couple of challenges

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:53.500
before we can
leverage the benefits

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:56.170
of that new technology.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:00.280
Firstly, the setup and
maintenance of robot fleets

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:03.040
today is typically
brought to the market

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:08.139
by system integrators that
create highly customized

00:02:08.139 --> 00:02:10.960
solution to individual clients.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:15.700
As a result, only large
industrial customers

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:20.650
can afford automation
and then mostly only

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:22.450
for highly repetitive tasks.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:31.680
Secondly, given this
highly customized nature

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:36.290
of integration, there is
a strong vendor lock-in.

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:39.470
If you want to renew
your robot fleet

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:43.970
or use different type of
robots, setup and maintenance

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:45.560
becomes extremely complex.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:54.240
Thirdly, most of the assets
used for automation use cases

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.620
are proprietary.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:03:00.480
Thus, it is hard for
both software developers

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:04.960
and hardware manufacturers
to scale the applications.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:10.020
And as a result, they are forced
to deploy bespoke solutions

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:13.100
for individual clients.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:17.000
Last but not least,
most of the solutions

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:22.130
are deployed only on-premise,
which hinders scalability,

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:26.790
flexibility, and efficiency.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:29.880
At Google Cloud,
we are dedicated

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.940
to handles those
challenges in order

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:38.400
to make automation easier
and more affordable.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.400
Our cloud automation
platform provides

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.950
foundational
capabilities for cloud

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.530
enabled automation
solutions that

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:52.620
are scalable, support large
data volumes and speed,

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:57.330
flexible, allowing
flexible distribution

00:03:57.330 --> 00:04:01.230
and deployment of
software assets,

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:06.120
and efficient, permit better
utilization and infrastructure

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.577
as a software provisioning.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:14.350
Our cloud automation
solution allows

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:20.230
companies that are interested
in the promise of Industrie 4.0

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:25.740
to turn their operations into
the competitive advantage.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:30.840
And the key word
here is flexibility,

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:35.910
that is the ability to
easily connect and operate

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:39.420
the fleet independently
of the vendor.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:45.760
One key technology behind
that is Kubernetes,

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:49.270
which builds on years
of experience of Google

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:56.320
in automatic deploying and
scaling software assets.

00:04:56.320 --> 00:05:00.580
We also address fundamental
security concepts,

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:05.000
such as authentication
and authorization.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:09.770
We also facilitate reliable
connectivity and communication

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:13.460
with synchronous and
unsynchronous communication.

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:18.030
And last but not least, we
provide critical infrastructure

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:22.330
for sensor data
aggregation and processing

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:26.760
that builds on familiar
technologies, such as, Bigtable

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:28.460
BigQuery, and DataFlow.

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:37.400
As mentioned, the key technology
behind that is Kubernetes.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:40.070
Using Kubernetes, we
enable the distribution

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:45.470
of containerized software assets
that can run on three tiers--

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:49.950
on robot, on-premise,
and in the cloud.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:54.780
We use Kubernetes to enable
robot hardware abstraction

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:57.270
and command and control
that is tolerant

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:59.310
to intermittent connectivity.

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:05.860
With Kubernetes technology,
we also create the opportunity

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:09.640
for third party developers
to quickly engage

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:12.840
with our platform
and develop on that.

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:24.040
On top of that, we want to
enable the vision of what we

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:27.210
started calling digital twin.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:31.170
This is the mirror
of the physical world

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:34.670
in the digital world.

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:38.480
Imagine the robot running
through that warehouse

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:43.290
and collecting the data
on inventory levels.

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:48.840
Exactly the same robot can run
through that warehouse and flag

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:53.370
damaged items, creating new
opportunities for quality

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:57.240
management and inventorization.

00:06:57.240 --> 00:07:03.260
That is, digital twin
and AI capabilities

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:06.450
with perception-driven
capabilities

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:09.900
open the whole set
of new opportunities

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:12.630
that go much beyond automation.

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:19.210
Last but not least,
on top of this,

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:22.120
all this critical
infrastructure, we

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:27.280
want to offer first party
services that leverage cloud

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:30.940
automation platform
and solve critical pain

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:35.370
points for the clients.

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:39.750
The first one is
localization and mapping

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:43.080
that uses data from
sensors like [? gliders ?]

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:44.970
and depth cameras.

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:48.660
It allows robots
to create a map,

00:07:48.660 --> 00:07:52.860
localize themselves on that map,
and recognize static landmarks.

00:07:57.460 --> 00:08:00.580
With our spatial
intelligence service,

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:05.620
we further want to analyze that
sensor data and semantically

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:10.480
understands that environment,
direct robots to rows,

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:14.050
shelves instead of just
metric coordinates.

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:22.500
Last but not least, with our
object intelligence service,

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:27.870
we can use the same data
to discover and identify

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:31.200
important objects and their
location in the work space

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:35.100
that allows robots to
perform certain operations

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:35.865
on those items.

00:08:42.059 --> 00:08:45.515
So how does all
that look in action?

00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:52.760
The best early implementation
of that technology

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:55.190
is Bechtle Logistics.

00:08:55.190 --> 00:08:58.430
That's where we
work with Bechtle,

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:02.780
SAP as a provider of
warehouse management system,

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:06.900
MIR, Mobile Industrial Robots,
the provider of hardware

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:10.910
a local robot fleet,
and Navvis, the enabler

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:13.800
of the digital twin.

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:17.790
But before I talk too
much about Bechtle,

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:21.810
I just want to invite Bechtle
itself on stage, Klaus Kratz,

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:25.650
the head of logistics
of Bechtle to tell you

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:30.150
about his experience and
how we are making impact

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:32.170
with our technology there.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:32.737
Welcome.

00:09:32.737 --> 00:09:33.570
Thank you very much.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:38.925
KLAUS KRATZ: Thank you.

00:09:38.925 --> 00:09:42.360
Ewa, thank you very much for
the introduction and having me.

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:47.510
I'm indeed very happy
to be in San Francisco.

00:09:47.510 --> 00:09:49.490
As you have mentioned,
we are from Germany.

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:54.200
And Germany is the country of
the thinkers and the poets.

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:58.880
So why I should be here in this
incredible innovative place?

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:03.110
Because I have adapt
your mentality,

00:10:03.110 --> 00:10:05.630
your spirit, the
American spirit just

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:09.710
to do whatever it takes
to gain new knowledge

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:11.240
and new competencies.

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:18.000
Also, that's why I'm
very enthusiastic to have

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:23.230
started this project with
Google, with Navvis, SAP,

00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:23.910
and MIR.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:30.400
At Bechtle, this
is our headquarter.

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:34.320
At Bechtle, I'm
responsible for logistics.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:37.550
We sell hardware, software,
IT solutions, and IT services

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:39.830
and of course, cloud services.

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:42.230
We are a European company.

00:10:42.230 --> 00:10:44.990
And we have partners
all over the world.

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:47.540
For example, PC Connection
in Massachusetts

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:50.150
is a partner of us in America.

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:52.910
We have more than
10,000 employees

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:59.270
and 17,000 happy customers.

00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:02.840
Bechtle is, in my opinion,
a German success story,

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:05.910
not at the scale of
Google of course.

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:15.050
But we have tripled our revenues
within the last 10 years

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:18.500
from 1.8 billion euro
to 4.2 billion euro.

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:20.720
And our target is
for the next 10 years

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:26.510
to double again this
turnover to 10 billion euro.

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:29.780
To reach this target, we have
to integrate our customers more

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:33.770
deeply, increase efficiency,
flexibility, and quality

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:36.740
within our processes
and systems,

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:40.030
and find ways to cooperate
with future strategic partners.

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:47.520
When the wind of change
blows, some people,

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:51.060
they build walls, others,
they build windmills,

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:53.400
and we are building windmills.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:58.860
So Bechtle Logistic has to
change from volume distribution

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.990
to solution distribution.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:03.330
On this way, we
already provide value

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:06.150
added services, such
as individual tagging,

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:09.810
packaging, repackaging,
and transporting

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:12.390
and also sustainable solution.

00:12:12.390 --> 00:12:14.460
Maybe in the near
future, we will

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:17.790
have a flat rate for
workplace, for all IT equipment

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:21.060
and software, customer needs,
including the recycling

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:22.640
and disposal of used hardware.

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:30.990
Currently, we have four main
warehouses-- the biggest

00:12:30.990 --> 00:12:32.160
warehouses in Germany.

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:34.290
We have other warehouses
in France, Switzerland

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:35.760
and Netherlands.

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:38.790
In the past, we had to
optimize and physically

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:41.550
alter our warehouses,
which require

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:45.300
a lot of time and improvisation
skills and a lot of money,

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:47.670
as you can see within
the next photos.

00:12:47.670 --> 00:12:51.270
And this is really reality.

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:54.770
So why we have this drilling
machine in our warehouse?

00:12:54.770 --> 00:12:58.430
Because we had to implement a
mezzanine within our warehouse.

00:12:58.430 --> 00:13:02.830
And we had to drill 30
holes 11 meters deep.

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:05.900
And this is really
logistical things.

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:06.860
It's really tough.

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:09.170
And we have done like
[? crystal ?] every night.

00:13:09.170 --> 00:13:16.400
We have covered our racks to
avoid dust of all our articles.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:19.280
And then you can
see the mezzanine.

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:23.780
It's 3 and 1/2
thousand square meters.

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:29.030
You see the white ellipse.

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:31.310
Behind this, there
are people working.

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:32.930
And an American
colleague said to me,

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:34.490
oh, this is very
bad, because it's

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:38.820
against security restrictions.

00:13:38.820 --> 00:13:42.930
So I've hidden these
two people there.

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:46.710
But you can see a stage,
a mezzanine is growing.

00:13:46.710 --> 00:13:49.040
And this is the
actual warehouse.

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:55.100
In the rack, we have big parts
like servers, PCs, notebooks.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:58.670
And on the mezzanine,
in we have small parts

00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:00.170
like cables and USB sticks.

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:07.830
In the future, we will need
many more warehouses in Germany

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:10.170
and also in Europe
with a possibility

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:14.160
to automate processes, adapt
them to customer requirements.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:17.100
We need in the future
very high flexibility,

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:20.170
dynamic scalability, and
very short throughputs

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:24.380
to deliver to our customer
as fast as possible.

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:27.920
Our customers can count
on us for the support

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:30.650
they need to reach their own
targets as they transition

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:33.530
to German Industry 4.0.

00:14:33.530 --> 00:14:36.020
The future warehouse,
in my opinion,

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:38.630
is a combination of
traditional technologies,

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:43.190
like high rack warehouse
systems and modern technologies,

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:46.215
or new technology like,
autonomous mobile robots.

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:52.790
In our warehouse,
as if I had said,

00:14:52.790 --> 00:14:57.860
we have already implemented the
Google SAP MIR Navvis solution.

00:14:57.860 --> 00:15:02.180
We are using the solution for
tasks such as cross-docking.

00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:05.670
Cross-docking items means
that in inbound logistics,

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:09.710
we get information from SAP,
but customer orders have already

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:12.080
been placed for these items.

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:15.380
Instead of processing
put-away and picking,

00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:20.450
we bring these items directly
to the outbound logistics.

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:24.170
In the past, we did this
with electrical vehicles

00:15:24.170 --> 00:15:25.550
on a pallet.

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:28.880
And now we are doing it with
racks, multi-level racks

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:31.170
and the robotics.

00:15:31.170 --> 00:15:34.395
And how it's working I
would show in a video.

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:41.400
So this is Claudio,
the MIR robot.

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:43.950
It's Claudio 1.

00:15:43.950 --> 00:15:45.840
With the support of
its sensors, Claudio

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:50.170
picks up the cart on which
are cross-docking items.

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:53.260
Claudio starts to
drive autonomously

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:57.260
to its designated destination.

00:15:57.260 --> 00:16:00.420
And Claudio drives
within a defined zone

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:03.960
and avoids barriers that may
occur on its way independently

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:05.080
by going around them.

00:16:12.100 --> 00:16:14.560
Claudio observes
the environment.

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:18.300
Still, our people have
got to get used to it.

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:22.360
In some critical areas with
cross traffic or forklifts,

00:16:22.360 --> 00:16:25.830
Claudio is emitting
sounds to get attention.

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:29.500
Claudio transports the cart
to its designated destination

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:30.820
and moves out for new tasks.

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:34.900
It's great.

00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:38.840
And this is a great team from
Google, SAP, and Bechtle.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:45.120
As a result of using
autonomous mobile robots

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:49.590
and future optimization, we can
achieve flexible automation,

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:52.620
process optimization,
scalability, and productivity.

00:16:56.190 --> 00:17:01.310
And I had a good example
from a forklift driver,

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:03.470
because we are very
transparent and if we

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:06.869
change to such new technologies,
we have an open communication,

00:17:06.869 --> 00:17:11.810
we speak with other people
and to persuade them

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:14.970
because we have an unemployment
rate of 2% in the region

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:16.079
I am working.

00:17:16.079 --> 00:17:20.780
So we have to be forced
automize our warehouses,

00:17:20.780 --> 00:17:23.690
because we don't
get any more people.

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:25.369
We have to qualify them.

00:17:25.369 --> 00:17:28.760
And so the people have
realized that this is possible.

00:17:28.760 --> 00:17:30.050
And they are not afraid.

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:32.510
And the forklift
driver, the next day, I

00:17:32.510 --> 00:17:35.390
have mentioned that we
go in this strategy.

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:37.760
He said to me,
but Mr. Kratz, you

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:39.530
have to pay attention
with the robotics,

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:41.630
because I don't
want to crash them

00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:44.940
So people immediately
think about--

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:47.990
and this is great
in my opinion--

00:17:47.990 --> 00:17:51.220
what will happen with
these new technologies?

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:54.180
And this is also the
adaption of the people

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:56.160
for these new technologies.

00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:59.380
So thank you very much
for your attention.

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:01.110
And if you are ever
in Germany, feel

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:03.572
free to come by and say hello.

00:18:03.572 --> 00:18:06.310
[APPLAUSE]

00:18:06.697 --> 00:18:08.280
EWA DUERR: Thank you
very much, Klaus,

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:12.750
for bringing your valuable
perspective to that audience

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:15.435
and sharing your experiences
with our project.

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:23.030
Thank you.

00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:23.655
We'll continue.

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:32.490
This is exactly the
best implementation

00:18:32.490 --> 00:18:36.316
of how we and our
partners, such as MIR,

00:18:36.316 --> 00:18:40.860
and Navvis, and SAP can make
an impact for businesses

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:43.250
like Bechtle.

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:47.300
In particular, we
need to make sure

00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:51.800
that we make automation
drastically simpler

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:54.630
and less expensive.

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:57.060
Our core value
proposition thus has

00:18:57.060 --> 00:19:01.320
to be flexible automation with
collaborative for robots that

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:06.930
can seamlessly and gradually
be deployed into the existing

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:08.760
environment as needed.

00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:16.510
Secondly, we need to escape
the vendor lock-in trap

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:21.330
and enable an easy deployment
of heterogeneous fleet

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:24.540
that are vendor agnostic.

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:27.060
Clients like Bechtle
shouldn't have

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:29.760
to take care of
coordinating the robots

00:19:29.760 --> 00:19:33.570
and processes between
different kinds of robots.

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:38.100
Rather, we should enable an
ERP system the assignment

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:42.240
of tasks and orders in
an intelligent manner

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:43.680
across various robots.

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:52.640
Thirdly, we now have a
chance to grow our impact

00:19:52.640 --> 00:19:57.200
by shaping new opportunities in
analytics, for example, quality

00:19:57.200 --> 00:20:00.230
management, inventorization,
space management, and so

00:20:00.230 --> 00:20:01.950
on and so forth.

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:05.770
By putting our AI
capabilities into action,

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:09.910
we will enable the
vision of digital twin,

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:14.740
generating new insights that
go much beyond pure automation.

00:20:18.030 --> 00:20:24.060
Finally, we need to break away
from purely on-prem solutions

00:20:24.060 --> 00:20:27.450
that are difficult
to scale and suffer

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:31.770
from limited flexibility in
low resource utilization.

00:20:31.770 --> 00:20:37.130
Rather, cloud automation
should use Kubernetes

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:39.710
to enable easy deployment
and distribution

00:20:39.710 --> 00:20:42.920
of containerized
software assets that

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:46.690
can run on-robot,
on-premise and in the cloud.

00:20:49.670 --> 00:20:58.260
With all that, we can
generate real business impact

00:20:58.260 --> 00:21:01.560
that allows fast
and easy automation

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:06.720
and enables the flexibility
in setting up and maintaining

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:09.710
automation processes.

00:21:09.710 --> 00:21:14.240
It facilitates efficiency
and increased utilization

00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:18.710
by efficient fleet management,
better and faster localization,

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.600
and optimized path planning.

00:21:23.270 --> 00:21:26.830
It also triggers
productivity improvements

00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:32.200
by turning analytics into action
and opening new opportunities

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:36.520
in inventory space and
quality management.

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:41.830
And last but not least, it
provides basis for scalability,

00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:45.340
competitiveness, and
better customer service

00:21:45.340 --> 00:21:50.200
that will allow businesses
to reap new revenue sources

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:52.050
and engage with new clients.

00:21:58.430 --> 00:22:03.490
But to enable all that vision
and leverage that technology,

00:22:03.490 --> 00:22:05.260
we need to work
with our partners

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:08.890
and grow that platform
into an ecosystem

00:22:08.890 --> 00:22:13.120
where each of the participants
can benefit and contribute,

00:22:13.120 --> 00:22:17.060
providing their
complementary skills.

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:20.110
That's why we
invited some of them

00:22:20.110 --> 00:22:26.190
today to share their experiences
with Cloud Automation Platform

00:22:26.190 --> 00:22:31.140
and explain to you how we
can all create new business

00:22:31.140 --> 00:22:34.010
opportunities for them.

00:22:34.010 --> 00:22:38.315
And on that note, I want to
invite on stage our partners.

00:22:45.740 --> 00:22:52.220
Nemrude Verzano, head
of Industry 4.0 at SAP,

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:55.790
he leads innovation
projects in the areas

00:22:55.790 --> 00:22:58.850
of logistics, manufacturing,
and retail and drives

00:22:58.850 --> 00:23:03.470
programs for the intelligent
enterprise strategy for SAP.

00:23:03.470 --> 00:23:05.520
Thank you very much
for being here.

00:23:05.520 --> 00:23:06.320
Walk on stage.

00:23:06.320 --> 00:23:11.680
